<title>SOUTH AFRICA: CRICKET-NORTHERNS CHASING 322 FOR VICTORY.</title>
<headline>CRICKET-NORTHERNS CHASING 322 FOR VICTORY.</headline>
<dateline>PORT ELIZABETH 1997-02-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Northern Transvaal will</p>
<p>resume their run chase of 322 for victory over Eastern Province</p>
<p>at St George's Park on Monday.</p>
<p>The visitors, however, were already two wickets down at the</p>
<p>close on Sunday on nine for two.</p>
<p>Having resumed their first innings in the morning on 152 for</p>
<p>two Northerns capitulated for 272 -- just 10 runs short of the</p>
<p>follow-on target.</p>
<p>Nevertheless, EP chose not to enforce the follow-on and lost</p>
<p>just two wickets in putting on a further 161 runs. Louis Koen</p>
<p>top scored with 75 from just 71 balls.</p>
<p>The home side having put on 432 for nine declared in their</p>
<p>first innings have always had the upper hand in this match and</p>
<p>are more likely to take the eight wickets they require for</p>
<p>victory than Northerns score the remaing 313 runs on a</p>
<p>deteriorating wcket.</p>
